## A) EXECUTIVE SYNTHESIS

### What We're Building

Treekipedia is the **only global tool that combines species prediction (37,800+ species after merge) with land-state-aware recommendations and carbon/biomass estimation**. At any point on Earth, it answers three distinct questions:

1. **"What is growing there now?"** — Current state estimation (disturbance, successional stage, composition)
2. **"What CAN grow there?"** — Biophysical suitability under current conditions
3. **"What SHOULD we grow there?"** — Strategy-constrained spatial optimization

These three questions must produce **separate outputs**, not blended into one ranking. This separation (from Codex) is the single most important architectural constraint for v3+.

